        "Fill the biggest saucepan you own with salted water and bring it to the boil over high heat. Pull the outer leaves off the cabbage and keep them, then drop the rest of it in whole. Let it boil three or four minutes, turning it if the water doesn't quite cover it.",
        "The blanching is the point here. A supermarket cabbage comes as a tight round ball, and because the leaves are crisp they snap and crack when you try to pull them off raw. A few minutes in boiling water and they come away whole, which is the only way this dish works.",
